[claude] 🔧 mcp__kernelgen__finalize_round: {"conclusion": {"round_num": 1, "expectation_status": "baseline", "root_cause": "Baseline established: the seed is un-importable (relative `..utils` import), so a self-contained generic index-space atomic kernel was measured instead. All 18 workloads pass, but the generic path costs 8 sequential int32 div/mod steps plus a 34-argument launch per element-block, giving 0.106x on the large cases (31.5ms vs 3.36ms reference for 2048^2) and only 0.54-0.64x on the 128^2 cases (0.26ms vs 0.14-0.17ms), where the two-launch host path dominates.", "perf_gap_analysis": "Frozen expectation was to establish a baseline, which was met quantitatively: geo_mean 0.1903, min_speedup 0.106 (scatter_add-timing-8). Workload-level split shows two distinct gaps: (1) large cases are per-element bound - candidate 7.5ns/element (1024^2: 7.91ms/1.05M) versus reference 0.81ns/element, i.e. ~9x slower per element, consistent with 8 runtime-valued div/mod steps per element and int32 address recomputation; (2) the 128^2 cases are fixed-overhead bound - 267us for 16K elements is far above the ~120us that per-element cost alone predicts, so roughly 140us is launch/host cost (two Triton launches with 34 and 4 runtime arguments), against a 170us reference walltime. Correctness passed with abs_err <= 0.03125 and matched_ratio 1.0 on all 9 correctness cases, so the generic ND indexing (front-padded 8-slot decomposition, dim stride zeroed plus idx*odim) is validated as the reference-correct fallback.", "next_suggestion": "Add a specialized last-dimension contiguous kernel for the timed shape family (contiguous inp/index/src, equal shapes, dim == ndim-1): a 2D grid (row, column-block) that computes offsets as row*ncols + col with no div/mod and only 4 runtime arguments, keeping the generic 8-slot kernel as the fallback for other dims, partial index extents and strided layouts. Expected to cut the per-element index arithmetic (large cases) and the launcher argument